{
  "format": "bp-relevance-controls/1",
  "description": "The control set: the frameworks and capabilities the system ALREADY has. Every coverage measurement carries these. If a control scores zero, the measurement failed and is discarded rather than reported. This is the rule that caught two of the three methods tried in Phase 1.",
  "why": "A measurement without a control cannot distinguish 'the thing is missing' from 'the method cannot see it'. The Phase 1 sweep read core-course lists and found nothing for any framework, including these — the control failed and the measurement was thrown away.",
